## 6. Main Backend Modules and What They Do

### 6.1 `backend/robot_app/main.py`
This is the main FastAPI application entry point.

It does important startup work:
- initializes settings,
- creates database tables,
- sets up CORS,
- includes all API routers,
- and serves the frontend build if it exists.

This file is the central hub for the backend.

### 6.2 `backend/robot_app/api/health.py`
Returns the health status of the app.

Example response includes:
- status,
- system name,
- app version,
- demo mode,
- timestamp,
- CPU usage,
- memory usage.

This tells you whether the server is alive and healthy.

### 6.3 `backend/robot_app/api/predict.py`
This is the prediction endpoint group for:
- sensor-only prediction,
- vision-only prediction,
- multimodal prediction,
- and demo/live simulation.

It takes user input and sends it to the model predictor.

### 6.4 `backend/robot_app/api/explain.py`
This provides explainability results.

It supports:
- SHAP explanations,
- Grad-CAM overlay generation,
- summary text for the model output.

This is critical because the project is not only a classifier—it is an explainable AI system.

### 6.5 `backend/robot_app/api/robustness.py`
This evaluates model performance under stress conditions.

It tests the system under:
- different noise levels,
- sensor dropout rates,
- and missing modality scenarios.

The goal is to measure how well the model behaves when the data quality is poor.

### 6.6 `backend/robot_app/api/safety.py`
This applies rule-based safety logic to model output.

It checks:
- confidence,
- severity,
- failure type,
- and system state,

then decides the recommended operator action such as:
- continue operation,
- reduce speed,
- schedule maintenance,
- or immediate halt.

### 6.7 `backend/robot_app/api/models.py`
This exposes model metadata and comparison information.

It is used by the model comparison page to show model performance across architectures.

### 6.8 `backend/robot_app/api/experiments.py`
This provides experiment details and benchmark logs.

It supports the experiments page so the user can review research data and experiment history.

### 6.9 `backend/robot_app/api/datasets.py`
This is used for dataset registration and upload.

It allows storing or cataloging:
- sensor CSV files,
- image datasets,
- or multimodal benchmark data.

The page shows dataset metadata, sample count, detected mapping, and storage location.

### 6.10 `backend/robot_app/api/train.py`
This endpoint(s) support model training and training status reporting.

It is used by the Training page in the dashboard.

### 6.11 `backend/robot_app/api/alerts.py`
This manages alerts from the system.

It allows:
- reading current alerts,
- updating them,
- and acknowledging them through the UI.

