## 9. Explainability in the Project

Explainability is a major focus. The project does not just say “fault detected”; it explains why.

### SHAP
SHAP is used to show which sensor features contributed most to the prediction. For example:
- vibration RMS,
- motor current,
- temperature drift,
- or signal variance.

This helps identify which input features most strongly affected the decision.

### Grad-CAM
Grad-CAM is used to show which region of the image influenced the model most.

This is especially useful for visual inspections because it can highlight the exact region of a part that appears defective.

### Why this matters
In industrial systems, operators need to trust the model. Explainability ensures the system is more transparent and easier to validate.

